<tr id="mwCXw">
<th id="mwCX0"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#Alabama" class="mw-selflink-fragment" id="mwCX4">Alabama</a></th>
<td data-sort-value="Yes" style="background: #DFD; color:black; vertical-align: middle; text-align: center; " class="table-yes2 skin-invert" typeof="mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt1026" id="mwCX8" data-mw='{"parts":["|data-sort-value=0 ",{"template":{"target":{"wt":"ya","href":"./Template:Ya"},"params":{"text":{"wt":"New districts enacted"}},"i":0}}]}'>New districts enacted</td>
<td id="mwCYA">In April 2026, the Supreme Court ruled on <i id="mwCYE"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louisiana_v._Callais" title="Louisiana v. Callais" id="mwCYI">Louisiana v. Callais</a></i> that stricter scrutiny had to be applied with regard to section 2 of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Voting_Rights_Act" title="Voting Rights Act" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCYM">Voting Rights Act</a>. Governor <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kay_Ivey" title="Kay Ivey" id="mwCYQ">Kay Ivey</a> was initially reluctant to call a special session after <i id="mwCYU"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Allen_v._Milligan" title="Allen v. Milligan" id="mwCYY">Allen v. Milligan</a></i>, but was lobbied to do so by the state attorney general and secretary of state, both of whom also filed emergency injunctions to lift the requirements levied on them by the federal courts.<sup about="#mwt1030" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-131" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-131"}}'><a href="#cite_note-131" id="mwCYc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCYg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCYk">[</span>120<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCYo">]</span></span></a></sup> <div class="paragraphbreak" style="margin-top:0.5em" about="#mwt1027" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCYs" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"pb","href":"./Template:Pb"},"params":{},"i":0}}]}'></div>The Supreme Court voted 6–3 to lift the stay, paving the way for state legislators to redraw.<sup about="#mwt1033" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-132" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-132"}}'><a href="#cite_note-132" id="mwCYw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCY0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCY4">[</span>121<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCY8">]</span></span></a></sup> On May 26, 2026, an Alabama court blocked the new map, arguing that the <i id="mwCZA"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louisiana_v._Callais" title="Louisiana v. Callais" id="mwCZE">Louisiana v. Callais</a></i> decision does not change the fact that the map intentionally discriminates against African-American voters in violation of the Constitution.<sup about="#mwt1036" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-133" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-133"}}'><a href="#cite_note-133" id="mwCZI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCZM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCZQ">[</span>122<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCZU">]</span></span></a></sup> On June 2, 2026, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supreme_Court_of_the_United_States" title="Supreme Court of the United States" id="mwCZY">Supreme Court</a> granted stay on the block, allowing the new map to be implemented.<sup about="#mwt1039" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-134" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-134"}}'><a href="#cite_note-134" id="mwCZc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCZg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCZk">[</span>123<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCZo">]</span></span></a></sup></td>
<td id="mwCZs"><span typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:File" about="#mwt1040" id="mwCZw" data-mw='{"caption":"Steady","parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"steady","href":"./Template:Steady"},"params":{},"i":0}}]}'><span title="Steady"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Steady2.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/20px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/40px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="Steady" data-file-width="300" data-file-height="300" data-file-type="drawing" height="11" width="11" class="mw-file-element"/></span></span></td>
