<tr id="mwCcM">
<th id="mwCcQ"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#Florida" class="mw-selflink-fragment" id="mwCcU">Florida</a></th>
<td data-sort-value="Yes" style="background: #DFD; color:black; vertical-align: middle; text-align: center; " class="table-yes2 skin-invert" typeof="mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt1057" id="mwCcY" data-mw='{"parts":["|data-sort-value=0 ",{"template":{"target":{"wt":"ya","href":"./Template:Ya"},"params":{"text":{"wt":"[[2026 Florida redistricting|New districts enacted]]"}},"i":0}}]}'><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Florida_redistricting" title="2026 Florida redistricting">New districts enacted</a></td>
<td id="mwCcc">In September 2023, a state circuit judge ruled that the map passed by the state legislature discriminated against Black voters, by redrawing the formerly plurality-Black 5th district to no longer have a Black plurality. Florida appealed this ruling and the map was reinstated by an appeals court.<sup about="#mwt1061" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-137" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-137"}}'><a href="#cite_note-137" id="mwCcg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCck"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCco">[</span>126<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCcs">]</span></span></a></sup><wbr id="mwCcw"/> In July 2025, the Florida Supreme Court ruled 5–1 to keep the current maps in place, finding that creating a plurality-Black congressional district would violate the federal <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Equal_Protection_Clause" title="Equal Protection Clause" id="mwCc0">Equal Protection Clause</a>.<sup about="#mwt1064" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-138" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-138"}}'><a href="#cite_note-138" id="mwCc4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCc8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCdA">[</span>127<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCdE">]</span></span></a></sup><div class="paragraphbreak" style="margin-top:0.5em" about="#mwt1058" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCdI" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"pb","href":"./Template:Pb"},"params":{},"i":0}}]}'></div>On January 9, 2026, Governor <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ron_DeSantis" title="Ron DeSantis" id="mwCdM">Ron DeSantis</a> called for a special session in April redrawing the state's congressional maps with the target of gaining 3 to 5 new Republican seats. However, Florida state law prevents deliberately redrawing congressional maps purely for partisan gain.<sup about="#mwt1067" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-139" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-139"}}'><a href="#cite_note-139" id="mwCdQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCdU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCdY">[</span>128<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCdc">]</span></span></a></sup> On February 27, 2026, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supreme_Court_of_Florida" title="Supreme Court of Florida" id="mwCdg">Supreme Court of Florida</a> rejected a petition to block the special session.<sup about="#mwt1070" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-140" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-140"}}'><a href="#cite_note-140" id="mwCdk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCdo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCds">[</span>129<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCdw">]</span></span></a></sup> On April 29, 2026, the maps were approved by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Florida_Legislature" title="Florida Legislature" id="mwCd0">Florida Legislature</a>.<sup about="#mwt1073" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-141" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-141"}}'><a href="#cite_note-141" id="mwCd4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCd8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCeA">[</span>130<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCeE">]</span></span></a></sup> On May 4, 2026, Governor DeSantis signed the new map into law.<sup about="#mwt1076" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-142" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-142"}}'><a href="#cite_note-142" id="mwCeI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCeM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCeQ">[</span>131<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCeU">]</span></span></a></sup></td>
<td id="mwCeY"><span typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:File" about="#mwt1077" id="mwCec" data-mw='{"caption":"Increase","parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"increase","href":"./Template:Increase"},"params":{},"i":0}}]}'><span title="Increase"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Increase2.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Increase2.svg/20px-Increase2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Increase2.svg/40px-Increase2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="Increase" data-file-width="300" data-file-height="300" data-file-type="drawing" height="11" width="11" class="mw-file-element"/></span></span> 1</td>
