<tr id="mwCwg">
<th id="mwCwk"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#Texas" class="mw-selflink-fragment" id="mwCwo">Texas</a></th>
<td data-sort-value="Yes" style="background: #DFD; color:black; vertical-align: middle; text-align: center; " class="table-yes2 skin-invert" typeof="mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt1212" id="mwCws" data-mw='{"parts":["|data-sort-value=0 ",{"template":{"target":{"wt":"ya","href":"./Template:Ya"},"params":{"text":{"wt":"[[2025 Texas redistricting|New districts enacted]]"}},"i":0}}]}'><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025_Texas_redistricting" title="2025 Texas redistricting">New districts enacted</a></td>
<td id="mwCww">In <i id="mwCw0">League of United Latin American Citizens v. Abbott</i>, held from May to June 2025 in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_District_Court_for_the_Western_District_of_Texas" title="United States District Court for the Western District of Texas" id="mwCw4">U.S. District Court for the Western District of Texas</a>, plaintiffs argued that the congressional districts passed by the state legislature discriminated against Black and Latino voters in violation of the Voting Rights Act.<sup about="#mwt1218" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-167" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-167"}}'><a href="#cite_note-167" id="mwCw8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCxA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCxE">[</span>156<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCxI">]</span></span></a></sup><div class="paragraphbreak" style="margin-top:0.5em" about="#mwt1213" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCxM" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"pb","href":"./Template:Pb"},"params":{},"i":0}}]}'></div><div class="paragraphbreak" style="margin-top:0.5em" about="#mwt1214" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCxQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"pb","href":"./Template:Pb"},"params":{},"i":0}}]}'></div>In early 2025, the Trump Administration urged Texas officials to redraw congressional districts. This was followed by a meeting of the Texas Republican congressional delegation to discuss mid-decade redistricting to secure extra Republican seats.<sup about="#mwt1221" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-168" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-168"}}'><a href="#cite_note-168" id="mwCxU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCxY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCxc">[</span>157<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCxg">]</span></span></a></sup> On July 9, Governor <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greg_Abbott" title="Greg Abbott" id="mwCxk">Greg Abbott</a> called a special session of the legislature to be held later that month with the goal of creating 5 new Republican seats. After Texas House Democrats staged a weeks-long walkout, the legislature passed the new maps on August 23, and Abbott signed them into law on August 29.<sup about="#mwt1222" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-tg_114-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"tg"}}'><a href="#cite_note-tg-114" id="mwCxo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCxs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCxw">[</span>104<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCx0">]</span></span></a></sup><div class="paragraphbreak" style="margin-top:0.5em" about="#mwt1215" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCx4" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"pb","href":"./Template:Pb"},"params":{},"i":0}}]}'></div> The previous case was paused, pending new maps.<sup about="#mwt1223" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-LULAC_110-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"LULAC"}}'><a href="#cite_note-LULAC-110" id="mwCx8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCyA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCyE">[</span>100<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCyI">]</span></span></a></sup> After passage, on August 27, the court scheduled a preliminary injunction hearing to begin on October 1 to October 10.<sup about="#mwt1226" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-oh_169-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"oh"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-oh-169"}}'><a href="#cite_note-oh-169" id="mwCyM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCyQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCyU">[</span>158<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCyY">]</span></span></a></sup> On November 18, the panel issued a preliminary injunction blocking the new map, putting the former map back in place. The case on the 2021 maps remains open, pending action from the U.S. Supreme Court in <i id="mwCyc"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louisiana_v._Callais" title="Louisiana v. Callais" id="mwCyg">Louisiana v. Callais</a></i>.<sup about="#mwt1227" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:5_115-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":5"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:5-115" id="mwCyk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCyo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCys">[</span>105<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCyw">]</span></span></a></sup> On November 21, the U.S. Supreme Court issued an administrative stay on the lower court ruling, temporarily leaving the new map in place.<sup about="#mwt1228" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-TXmap_116-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"TXmap"}}'><a href="#cite_note-TXmap-116" id="mwCy0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCy4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCy8">[</span>106<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCzA">]</span></span></a></sup> On December 4, the Supreme Court ruled 6–3 in allowing the map to stand for the 2026 elections.<sup about="#mwt1231" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-170" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-170"}}'><a href="#cite_note-170" id="mwCzE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCzI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCzM">[</span>159<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCzQ">]</span></span></a></sup></td>
<td data-sort-value="1" id="mwCzU"><span typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:File" about="#mwt1232" id="mwCzY" data-mw='{"caption":"Decrease","parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"decrease","href":"./Template:Decrease"},"params":{},"i":0}}]}'><span title="Decrease"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Decrease2.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Decrease2.svg/20px-Decrease2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Decrease2.svg/40px-Decrease2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="Decrease" data-file-width="300" data-file-height="300" data-file-type="drawing" height="11" width="11" class="mw-file-element"/></span></span> 3</td>
<td data-sort-value="0" id="mwCzc"><span typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:File" about="#mwt1233" id="mwCzg" data-mw='{"caption":"Decrease","parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"decrease","href":"./Template:Decrease"},"params":{},"i":0}}]}'><span title="Decrease"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Decrease2.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Decrease2.svg/20px-Decrease2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Decrease2.svg/40px-Decrease2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="Decrease" data-file-width="300" data-file-height="300" data-file-type="drawing" height="11" width="11" class="mw-file-element"/></span></span> 2</td>
<td data-sort-value="−1" id="mwCzk"><span typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:File" about="#mwt1234" id="mwCzo" data-mw='{"caption":"Increase","parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"increase","href":"./Template:Increase"},"params":{},"i":0}}]}'><span title="Increase"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Increase2.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Increase2.svg/20px-Increase2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Increase2.svg/40px-Increase2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="Increase" data-file-width="300" data-file-height="300" data-file-type="drawing" height="11" width="11" class="mw-file-element"/></span></span> 5</td></tr>
<tr id="mwCzs">
<th id="mwCzw"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#Utah" class="mw-selflink-fragment" id="mwCz0">Utah</a></th>
<td data-sort-value="Yes" style="background: #DFD; color:black; vertical-align: middle; text-align: center; " class="table-yes2 skin-invert" typeof="mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt1235" id="mwCz4" data-mw='{"parts":["|data-sort-value=0 ",{"template":{"target":{"wt":"ya","href":"./Template:Ya"},"params":{"text":{"wt":"New districts enacted"}},"i":0}}]}'>New districts enacted</td>
<td id="mwCz8">In July 2023, in <i id="mwC0A"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/League_of_Women_Voters_v._Utah_State_Legislature" title="League of Women Voters v. Utah State Legislature" id="mwC0E">League of Women Voters v. Utah State Legislature</a></i>, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Utah_Supreme_Court" title="Utah Supreme Court" id="mwC0I">Utah Supreme Court</a> heard arguments alleging that the Utah Legislature violated <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2018_Utah_Proposition_4" title="2018 Utah Proposition 4" id="mwC0M">a citizen-passed anti-gerrymandering proposition</a> by dividing Salt Lake County voters into all four of Utah's districts. The case was sent back to a state district court, which held a hearing in January 2025. A ruling for the League of Women Voters was issued on August 25. New maps were expected to be drawn up by the Legislature by September 24 and finalized by November.<sup about="#mwt1238" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-redrawn_171-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"redrawn"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-redrawn-171"}}'><a href="#cite_note-redrawn-171" id="mwC0Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC0U"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC0Y">[</span>160<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC0c">]</span></span></a></sup>
<div class="paragraphbreak" style="margin-top:0.5em" about="#mwt1239" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwC0g" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"pb","href":"./Template:Pb"},"params":{},"i":0}}]}'></div>On October 6, the Utah Legislature passed a new map, which changed 2 Republican districts to be more competitive.<sup about="#mwt1242" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:2_172-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":2"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:2-172"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:2-172" id="mwC0k"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC0o"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC0s">[</span>161<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC0w">]</span></span></a></sup> On November 10, Utah Third District Judge Dianna Gibson ruled that the new map also violated Proposition 4, opting to approve a plaintiff-submitted alternative, Map 1, which creates a safe Democratic district comprising only <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salt_Lake_County" title="Salt Lake County" class="mw-redirect" id="mwC00">Salt Lake County</a>.<sup about="#mwt1243" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:4_111-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":4"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:4-111" id="mwC04"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC08"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC1A">[</span>101<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC1E">]</span></span></a></sup></td>
<td id="mwC1I"><span typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:File" about="#mwt1244" id="mwC1M" data-mw='{"caption":"Increase","parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"increase","href":"./Template:Increase"},"params":{},"i":0}}]}'><span title="Increase"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Increase2.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Increase2.svg/20px-Increase2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Increase2.svg/40px-Increase2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="Increase" data-file-width="300" data-file-height="300" data-file-type="drawing" height="11" width="11" class="mw-file-element"/></span></span> 1</td>
<td id="mwC1Q"><span typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:File" about="#mwt1245" id="mwC1U" data-mw='{"caption":"Steady","parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"steady","href":"./Template:Steady"},"params":{},"i":0}}]}'><span title="Steady"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Steady2.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/20px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/40px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="Steady" data-file-width="300" data-file-height="300" data-file-type="drawing" height="11" width="11" class="mw-file-element"/></span></span></td>
<td id="mwC1Y"><span typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:File" about="#mwt1246" id="mwC1c" data-mw='{"caption":"Decrease","parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"decrease","href":"./Template:Decrease"},"params":{},"i":0}}]}'><span title="Decrease"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Decrease2.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Decrease2.svg/20px-Decrease2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Decrease2.svg/40px-Decrease2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="Decrease" data-file-width="300" data-file-height="300" data-file-type="drawing" height="11" width="11" class="mw-file-element"/></span></span> 1</td></tr>
<tr id="mwC1g">
<th id="mwC1k"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#Virginia" class="mw-selflink-fragment" id="mwC1o">Virginia</a></th>
<td style="background: #FFE3E3; color: black; vertical-align: middle; text-align: center; " class="table-no2 skin-invert" typeof="mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt1247" id="mwC1s" data-mw='{"parts":["|",{"template":{"target":{"wt":"no2","href":"./Template:No2"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Districts left in place"}},"i":0}}]}'>Districts left in place</td>
<td id="mwC1w">Democratic state lawmakers announced a plan to alter the state constitution to draw a new congressional map before the 2026 elections making 3–4 more Democratic seats.<sup about="#mwt1248" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-auto_125-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"auto"}}'><a href="#cite_note-auto-125" id="mwC10"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC14"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC18">[</span>115<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC2A">]</span></span></a></sup>
<div class="paragraphbreak" style="margin-top:0.5em" about="#mwt1249" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwC2E" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"pb","href":"./Template:Pb"},"params":{},"i":0}}]}'></div>The proposed mechanism was an amendment to the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constitution_of_Virginia" title="Constitution of Virginia" id="mwC2I">Constitution of Virginia</a> allowing the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Virginia_General_Assembly" title="Virginia General Assembly" id="mwC2M">General Assembly</a> to modify the state's congressional districts if any other state did so between January 1, 2025, and October 31, 2030, for any reason other than normal decennial redistricting or to satisfy a court order. Redistricting was transferred from the General Assembly to a bipartisan commission in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2020_Virginia_Question_1" title="2020 Virginia Question 1" id="mwC2Q">2020</a>, and the power would revert to the commission for the normal 2030 cycle. The amendment proposal first passed the General Assembly on October 31, 2025. The amendment procedure requires any proposal to pass in both houses of the General Assembly, then it must pass both houses again after the next <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Virginia_House_of_Delegates" title="Virginia House of Delegates" id="mwC2U">Virginia House of Delegates</a> election is held (every two years), then it must be approved in a referendum.<sup about="#mwt1252" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-173" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-173"}}'><a href="#cite_note-173" id="mwC2Y"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC2c"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC2g">[</span>162<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC2k">]</span></span></a></sup>

<p id="mwC2o"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Virginia_Senate" title="Virginia Senate" id="mwC2s">Virginia Senate</a> minority leader <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ryan_McDougle" title="Ryan McDougle" id="mwC2w">Ryan McDougle</a>, a Republican, sued Democratic House Speaker <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Don_Scott_(Virginia_politician)" title="Don Scott (Virginia politician)" id="mwC20">Don Scott</a> over the legality of the amendment. On January 27, 2026, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tazewell_County,_Virginia" title="Tazewell County, Virginia" id="mwC24">Tazewell County</a> Circuit Court Judge Jack Hurley, Jr. ruled that the amendment could not satisfy the intervening-election requirement since early voting in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025_Virginia_elections" title="2025 Virginia elections" id="mwC28">2025 Virginia elections</a> was underway at the time of passage.<sup about="#mwt1255" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-174" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-174"}}'><a href="#cite_note-174" id="mwC3A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC3E"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC3I">[</span>163<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC3M">]</span></span></a></sup> On January 28, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_of_Virginia" title="Democratic Party of Virginia" id="mwC3Q">Democratic Party of Virginia</a> appealed the ruling; the court of appeals, citing the importance of the case, forwarded it to the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supreme_Court_of_Virginia" title="Supreme Court of Virginia" id="mwC3U">Supreme Court of Virginia</a> for an expedited ruling on February 4.<sup about="#mwt1258" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-175" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-175"}}'><a href="#cite_note-175" id="mwC3Y"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC3c"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC3g">[</span>164<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC3k">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1261" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-176" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-176"}}'><a href="#cite_note-176" id="mwC3o"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC3s"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC3w">[</span>165<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC30">]</span></span></a></sup> On February 10, the General Assembly passed the amendment proposal the required second time and included a draft map that would likely net Democrats four seats.<sup about="#mwt1264" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-177" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-177"}}'><a href="#cite_note-177" id="mwC34"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC38"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC4A">[</span>166<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC4E">]</span></span></a></sup> On February 13, the Supreme Court allowed the April 21 <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Virginia_redistricting_amendment" title="2026 Virginia redistricting amendment" class="mw-redirect" id="mwC4I">referendum</a> to go forward while it considered the matter. The referendum passed with 51.7% voting yes.<sup about="#mwt1267" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-178" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-178"}}'><a href="#cite_note-178" id="mwC4M"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC4Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC4U">[</span>167<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC4Y">]</span></span></a></sup> The next day, Judge Hurley ruled the referendum to be unconstitutional on the basis of another lawsuit and enjoined the state board of elections from certifying the result. Attorney General <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jay_Jones" title="Jay Jones" id="mwC4c">Jay Jones</a> appealed the decision; the Supreme Court declined to stay it while the original case was ongoing and as a result the board was unable to certify the result at its May meeting.<sup about="#mwt1270" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-179" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-179"}}'><a href="#cite_note-179" id="mwC4g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC4k"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC4o">[</span>168<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC4s">]</span></span></a></sup> <sup about="#mwt1273" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-180" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-180"}}'><a href="#cite_note-180" id="mwC4w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC40"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC44">[</span>169<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC48">]</span></span></a></sup> The Supreme Court heard oral arguments in the case on April 27.<sup about="#mwt1276" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-181" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-181"}}'><a href="#cite_note-181" id="mwC5A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC5E"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC5I">[</span>170<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC5M">]</span></span></a></sup></p> 

On May 8, the Supreme Court invalidated the amendment in a 4–3 decision, with the majority agreeing with Judge Hurley's ruling that its first passage was too late to satisfy the intervening-election requirement.<sup about="#mwt1280" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-182" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-182"}}'><a href="#cite_note-182" id="mwC5Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC5U"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC5Y">[</span>171<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC5c">]</span></span></a></sup><div class="paragraphbreak" style="margin-top:0.5em" about="#mwt1277" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwC5g" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"pb","href":"./Template:Pb"},"params":{},"i":0}}]}'></div>Following the ruling, Speaker Scott and Attorney General Jones filed an emergency appeal to the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Supreme_Court" title="United States Supreme Court" class="mw-redirect" id="mwC5k">United States Supreme Court</a>.<sup about="#mwt1283" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-183" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-183"}}'><a href="#cite_note-183" id="mwC5o"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC5s"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC5w">[</span>172<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC50">]</span></span></a></sup> On May 15, the Supreme Court denied the appeal.<sup about="#mwt1286" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-184" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-184"}}'><a href="#cite_note-184" id="mwC54"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC58"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC6A">[</span>173<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC6E">]</span></span></a></sup></td>
<td data-sort-value="1" id="mwC6I"><span typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:File" about="#mwt1287" id="mwC6M" data-mw='{"caption":"Steady","parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Same","href":"./Template:Same"},"params":{},"i":0}}]}'><span title="Steady"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Steady2.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/20px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/40px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="Steady" data-file-width="300" data-file-height="300" data-file-type="drawing" height="11" width="11" class="mw-file-element"/></span></span></td>
