<td id="mwC6w">In July 2025, a lawsuit was filed by two liberal law firms in a Wisconsin district court, asking to consider the constitutionality of Wisconsin's congressional maps.<sup about="#mwt1293" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-185" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-185"}}'><a href="#cite_note-185" id="mwC60"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC64"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC68">[</span>174<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC7A">]</span></span></a></sup> In September 2025, the Wisconsin Supreme court addressed this lawsuit and asked each party to provide briefs on whether this court case should proceed.<sup about="#mwt1296" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-186" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-186"}}'><a href="#cite_note-186" id="mwC7E"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC7I"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC7M">[</span>175<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC7Q">]</span></span></a></sup> On March 31, 2026, a judicial panel dismissed the challenge.<sup about="#mwt1299" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-187" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-187"}}'><a href="#cite_note-187" id="mwC7U"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC7Y"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC7c">[</span>176<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC7g">]</span></span></a></sup></td>
